   array['barbell']::text[],
   'time',
   'Alexander honors Staff Sgt. Alexander G. Povilaitis, 47, of Dawsonville, Georgia, of the 570th Sapper Company, 14th Engineer Battalion, 555th Brigade. He was killed in action on May 31, 2012, in Kandahar Province, Afghanistan, when an improvised explosive device struck his vehicle.

You complete five rounds of 31 back squats (135 lb / 95 lb) and 12 power cleans (185 lb / 125 lb). That is 155 back squats and 60 power cleans. The squat load is moderate, but 31 reps a round means long sets with the bar on your back, and the cleans are heavy enough that tired legs make every rep a fight. Most people need two bars set up side by side.',
   '[{"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "31", "tip": "Take the bar from a rack or clean it up and get it onto your back. Break the set before your form slips, such as 11, 10, 10.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Power Cleans", "reps": "12", "tip": "Quick singles with a fast turn of the elbows are safer than touch-and-go reps on tired legs.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Set up two bars so you never change plates", "Plan your squat sets before you start", "Singles on the cleans are fine"]'::jsonb,
   '["Load one bar for squats in a rack and one for cleans on the floor so you can move straight between them.", "Keep your chest up and push your knees out on every squat, even late in a set.", "Breathe at the top of each squat and rest with the bar on your back only if your position is solid.", "On the power cleans, keep the bar close and finish with your elbows high and fast.", "Aim for similar round times, since going too hard in round one makes the last two rounds very slow."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the squats to 95 lb / 65 lb and the power cleans to 135 lb / 95 lb, or pick loads you can squat for about 15 reps unbroken and clean for 5. Replace back squats with goblet squats or air squats if needed. Cut to three rounds if five would take more than about 40 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Alexander workout?", "answer": "5 rounds for time of 31 back squats (135 lb / 95 lb) and 12 power cleans (185 lb / 125 lb)."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Alexander?", "answer": "155 back squats and 60 power cleans."}, {"question": "Can I use one barbell for Alexander?", "answer": "You can, but you will spend time changing plates every round. Two bars, one in a rack for squats and one on the floor for cleans, keeps the workout moving."}, {"question": "Who was Alexander?", "answer": "Staff Sgt. Alexander G. Povilaitis, 47, of the 570th Sapper Company, 14th Engineer Battalion, 555th Brigade. He was killed in action on May 31, 2012, in Kandahar Province, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FIvEGQCfByc'),
  ('Andy',
   'andy',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   'For Time',
   '40–60 min',
   'advanced',
   'full-body',
   array['barbell','box','running','weightedVest']::text[],
   'time',
   'Andy honors U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Andrew T. Weathers, 30, of DeRidder, Louisiana, of the 2nd Battalion, 7th Special Forces Group. He was wounded on Sept. 28, 2014, in Helmand Province, Afghanistan, when he ran to a rooftop under heavy fire to stop an attack, saving the lives of five Green Berets and nine Afghan Commandos, and died two days later in Germany.

The whole workout is done in a weighted vest (20 lb / 14 lb). You go 25 thrusters, 50 box jumps (24 in / 20 in) and 75 deadlifts with a 115 lb / 75 lb barbell, run 1.5 miles, then repeat the barbell and box work in reverse. That is 50 thrusters, 100 box jumps and 150 deadlifts. The vest makes every part harder, and the second half starts on tired legs.',
   '[{"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "25", "tip": "Wear the vest for the whole workout. Break into sets of 5 to 8 and use your legs to drive the bar up.", "rx_men": "115 lb", "rx_women": "75 lb"}, {"name": "Box Jumps", "reps": "50", "tip": "Step down on every rep. The vest makes rebounding hard on your calves and Achilles.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "75", "tip": "Same bar as the thrusters. Sets of 10 to 15 with short rests keep your back fresh.", "rx_men": "115 lb", "rx_women": "75 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1.5 miles", "tip": "Run in the vest. Hold a steady pace and use the run to recover your grip.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "14 lb vest"}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "75", "tip": "Your grip will be tired after the run, so break sooner than you did the first time.", "rx_men": "115 lb", "rx_women": "75 lb"}, {"name": "Box Jumps", "reps": "50", "tip": "Step-ups are a smart choice here if your legs are failing.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "25", "tip": "The last 25. Small sets and short rests get you to the finish.", "rx_men": "115 lb", "rx_women": "75 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Wear the vest from start to finish", "Same bar for thrusters and deadlifts", "Run the 1.5 miles at a pace you can hold"]'::jsonb,
   '["Fit the vest snugly before you start so it does not bounce on the run or the box jumps.", "Plan your sets for the 75 deadlifts, such as five sets of 15, and keep the rests short.", "On the thrusters, catch the bar in a full front rack and drive up with your legs, not your arms.", "Treat the run as part recovery, part work. Going out too fast will cost you more on the second half.", "Expect the second set of deadlifts to be the hardest part, and break them into small sets early."]'::jsonb,
   'Leave out the vest or use a lighter one. Lower the barbell to 75 lb / 55 lb, use a 20 in / 16 in box or step up, and run 1 mile instead of 1.5. To shorten the workout, halve the reps on each side: 13 thrusters, 25 box jumps and 38 deadlifts.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Andy workout?", "answer": "Wearing a 20 lb / 14 lb vest, for time: 25 thrusters, 50 box jumps, 75 deadlifts, a 1.5-mile run, 75 deadlifts, 50 box jumps and 25 thrusters. The barbell is 115 lb / 75 lb and the box is 24 in / 20 in."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Andy?", "answer": "50 thrusters, 100 box jumps and 150 deadlifts, plus a 1.5-mile run."}, {"question": "Do I need a weighted vest for Andy?", "answer": "The Rx version uses a 20 lb vest for men and a 14 lb vest for women. You can do it without one as a scaled version."}, {"question": "Who was Andy?", "answer": "U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Andrew T. Weathers, 30, of the 2nd Battalion, 7th Special Forces Group. He was wounded in Helmand Province, Afghanistan, and died on Sept. 30, 2014, at Landstuhl Regional Medical Center in Germany."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8PLi4eOM68g'),
  ('Artie',
   'artie',
   'hero',
   null,
   'AMRAP 20',
   'AMRAP 20',
   '20 min',
   'intermediate',
   'full-body',
   array['pullUpBar','barbell','bodyweight']::text[],
   'rounds_reps',
   'Artie honors Police Officer Arthur "Artie" Lopez, 29, of Babylon Village, New York, a decorated eight-year veteran on the Nassau County Police Department''s Emergency Services Unit. He was killed in the line of duty on Oct. 23, 2012. He trained at CrossFit Merrick, and Fran and Cindy were among his favorite workouts.

In 20 minutes you complete as many rounds as you can of 5 pull-ups, 10 push-ups, 15 air squats, 5 more pull-ups and 10 thrusters (95 lb / 65 lb). The first half is Cindy, and the pull-ups and thrusters are the moves from Fran. Each round is 45 reps, and the second set of pull-ups and the thrusters get harder every round.',
   '[{"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "5", "tip": "The chin clears the bar on every rep. Keep these unbroken as long as you can."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "10", "tip": "Chest to the floor and a straight body line. Break early, such as 5 and 5."}, {"name": "Air Squats", "reps": "15", "tip": "Hips below the knees. Use them to catch your breath."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "5", "tip": "The second set comes on tired arms. Shake out your grip on the way to the bar."}, {"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "10", "tip": "Full squat, then drive the bar overhead to lockout. Keep it in sets of 5 or 10.", "rx_men": "95 lb", "rx_women": "65 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps in 20 minutes.',
   '["Keep the bar and pull-up bar close together", "Break push-ups before you fail", "Count your rounds as you go"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set the barbell right next to the pull-up bar so each transition takes a few seconds.", "Find a pace in the first two rounds that you can repeat for the full 20 minutes.", "Start breaking the push-ups early, since they tend to fall apart first.", "On the thrusters, let your legs do the work and press the bar through to full lockout.", "Keep a tally of rounds with chalk or a counter so your score is accurate."]'::jsonb,
   'Use jumping or banded pull-ups, push-ups on your knees or on a box, and a lighter barbell such as 65 lb / 45 lb. If you can''t do thrusters with a bar, use dumbbells or a light wall ball. The goal is to keep moving for the full 20 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Artie workout?", "answer": "As many rounds and reps as possible in 20 minutes of 5 pull-ups, 10 push-ups, 15 air squats, 5 pull-ups and 10 thrusters (95 lb / 65 lb)."}, {"question": "How many reps are in one round of Artie?", "answer": "45 reps: 10 pull-ups, 10 push-ups, 15 air squats and 10 thrusters."}, {"question": "How is Artie scored?", "answer": "Your score is the total rounds plus any extra reps you finish in 20 minutes."}, {"question": "Who was Artie?", "answer": "Police Officer Arthur \"Artie\" Lopez, 29, of the Nassau County Police Department''s Emergency Services Unit in New York. He was killed in the line of duty on Oct. 23, 2012."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qCkknGuPels'),
