   array['running','barbell','pullUpBar']::text[],
   'rounds_reps',
   'Barraza honors U.S. Army Staff Sgt. Ricardo Barraza, 24, of Shafter, California, of the 2nd Battalion, 75th Ranger Regiment. He died on March 18, 2006, in Ar Ramadi, Iraq, when he came under small-arms fire during combat operations.

In 18 minutes you complete as many rounds as you can of a 200 m run, 9 deadlifts (275 lb / 185 lb) and 6 burpee bar muscle-ups. The run is short, but the deadlifts are heavy and the burpee bar muscle-ups need both power and skill when you are out of breath. Your grip takes a beating from the deadlifts and the bar, so pacing matters from the first round.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "200 m", "tip": "Run fast but controlled. You need to arrive at the bar ready to lift."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "9", "tip": "Heavy. Use quick singles or sets of 3 with a tight brace and the bar close.", "rx_men": "275 lb", "rx_women": "185 lb"}, {"name": "Burpee Bar Muscle-Ups", "reps": "6", "tip": "Do a burpee facing the bar, jump to it and do a bar muscle-up. Take a breath before each jump."}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps in 18 minutes.',
   '["Set the bar near the start of the run", "Singles on the deadlifts are fine", "Rest before each muscle-up attempt rather than missing"]'::jsonb,
   '["Put the barbell and the pull-up bar near the start of the run so each round flows.", "On the deadlifts, set your back and push the floor away on every rep. Drop the bar under control rather than letting your back round.", "Take one breath after each burpee before you jump to the bar, since missed muscle-ups cost more time than a short pause.", "Keep a tight hollow-to-arch swing on the muscle-ups and pull the bar to your hips.", "Try to keep every round within a few seconds of the first."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the deadlift to 185 lb / 135 lb or less. Replace the burpee bar muscle-ups with burpee chest-to-bar pull-ups, burpee pull-ups or burpees plus jumping pull-ups. Keep the 200 m run, or row 250 m if you can''t run.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Barraza workout?", "answer": "As many rounds and reps as possible in 18 minutes of a 200 m run, 9 deadlifts (275 lb / 185 lb) and 6 burpee bar muscle-ups."}, {"question": "What is a burpee bar muscle-up?", "answer": "A burpee done facing the pull-up bar, followed by a jump to the bar and a bar muscle-up. Each one counts as one rep."}, {"question": "How is Barraza scored?", "answer": "Your score is the total rounds plus any extra reps you finish in 18 minutes."}, {"question": "Who was Barraza?", "answer": "U.S. Army Staff Sgt. Ricardo Barraza, 24, of the 2nd Battalion, 75th Ranger Regiment. He died on March 18, 2006, in Ar Ramadi, Iraq."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AIc6txJ3g0E'),
  ('Bell',
   'bell',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   '3 Rounds For Time',
   '15–25 min',
   'advanced',
   'full-body',
   array['barbell','pullUpBar']::text[],
   'time',
   'Bell honors Air Force Senior Airman Bryan R. Bell, 23, of Erie, Pennsylvania, of the 2nd Civil Engineer Squadron at Barksdale Air Force Base, Louisiana. He died on Jan. 5, 2012, at Camp Bastion in Afghanistan, of injuries suffered when his vehicle struck an improvised explosive device.

You complete three rounds of 21 deadlifts, 15 pull-ups and 9 front squats, all with one barbell (185 lb / 125 lb). That is 63 deadlifts, 45 pull-ups and 27 front squats. The deadlifts and pull-ups both drain your grip, and the front squats need a strong rack and an upright chest after your back is already tired. Moving between the bar and the rig quickly keeps the time down.',
   '[{"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "21", "tip": "Break into sets, such as 8, 7, 6, before your back position slips.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "15", "tip": "The chin clears the bar. Small sets of 5 protect your grip after the deadlifts."}, {"name": "Front Squats", "reps": "9", "tip": "Clean the bar up, keep your elbows high and stay upright. Sets of 5 and 4 work well.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["One bar for the whole workout", "Small pull-up sets save your grip", "Elbows high on the front squats"]'::jsonb,
   '["Plan your deadlift sets before the clock starts and stick to them.", "Keep the bar close and your lats tight on the deadlifts so your lower back stays neutral.", "Shake out your hands on the walk to the pull-up bar.", "Clean the bar into a solid front rack before your first front squat, and drive your elbows up as you stand.", "The last round of deadlifts is where the time is lost, so save a little in rounds one and two."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the barbell to 135 lb / 95 lb, or choose a load you can front squat for 9 reps in two sets. Use banded or jumping pull-ups, or ring rows. Cut the reps to 15-10-6 per round if you want a shorter workout.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Bell workout?", "answer": "3 rounds for time of 21 deadlifts, 15 pull-ups and 9 front squats, with one barbell at 185 lb / 125 lb."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Bell?", "answer": "63 deadlifts, 45 pull-ups and 27 front squats."}, {"question": "Do I use the same weight for the deadlifts and front squats?", "answer": "Yes. Bell uses one barbell for both lifts, 185 lb for men and 125 lb for women."}, {"question": "Who was Bell?", "answer": "Air Force Senior Airman Bryan R. Bell, 23, of the 2nd Civil Engineer Squadron at Barksdale Air Force Base. He died on Jan. 5, 2012, at Camp Bastion in Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RiBRIbuczMM'),
