   'time',
   'Brehm honors U.S. Army Sgt. Dale G. Brehm, 23, of Turlock, California, of the 2nd Battalion, 75th Ranger Regiment. He died on March 18, 2006, when he came under small-arms fire during combat operations in Ar Ramadi, Iraq.

This is a four-part chipper done once through: 10 rope climbs to 15 feet, 20 back squats (225 lb / 155 lb), 30 handstand push-ups and a 40-calorie row. Each part hits a different area. The rope climbs drain your grip and arms, the back squats are heavy for 20 reps, and the handstand push-ups come when your shoulders are already tired from the rope. The row at the end is a test of what you have left.',
   '[{"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "10", "tip": "Use a strong foot lock so your legs do the work and your grip lasts.", "rx_men": "15 ft", "rx_women": "15 ft"}, {"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "20", "tip": "Heavy for 20. Break into sets of 4 or 5 and keep your chest up.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}, {"name": "Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "30", "tip": "Head to the floor and arms locked at the top. Small sets from the start."}, {"name": "Row for Calories", "reps": "40 cal", "tip": "Push hard with your legs. Your arms will be tired from the climbs and push-ups."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Foot lock on every rope climb", "Small sets on the squats", "Break the handstand push-ups early"]'::jsonb,
   '["Control the descent on each rope climb instead of sliding, and shake out your hands between reps.", "Rack the bar for the back squats so you don''t have to get 225 lb / 155 lb onto your back from the floor.", "Plan short sets on the squats, such as 4 sets of 5, with short rests.", "On the handstand push-ups, sets of 3 to 5 before failure keep you moving.", "Set the rower damper before you start so you can go straight into the row."]'::jsonb,
   'Replace rope climbs with half climbs, lying rope pulls or pull-ups. Lower the back squat to 135 lb / 95 lb. Use pike push-ups or box pike push-ups for the handstand push-ups. Keep the 40-calorie row, or cut it to 30.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Brehm workout?", "answer": "For time: 10 rope climbs to 15 feet, 20 back squats (225 lb / 155 lb), 30 handstand push-ups and a 40-calorie row."}, {"question": "What is the hardest part of Brehm?", "answer": "For most people it is the handstand push-ups, because they come after the rope climbs have tired your arms and shoulders."}, {"question": "Can I do Brehm without a rope?", "answer": "Yes. Use pull-ups, lying rope pulls or towel pull-ups in place of the climbs, about 3 pull-ups per climb."}, {"question": "Who was Brehm?", "answer": "U.S. Army Sgt. Dale G. Brehm, 23, of the 2nd Battalion, 75th Ranger Regiment. He died on March 18, 2006, in Ar Ramadi, Iraq."}]'::jsonb,
