   'time',
   'Bruck honors U.S. Coast Guard Petty Officer 3rd Class Nathan B. Bruckenthal, 24, of Smithtown, New York, of Tactical Law Enforcement Team South, based at Coast Guard Air Station Miami. He was killed on April 24, 2004, at the Khawr Al Amaya Oil Terminal off the coast of Iraq, when a boat his team intercepted exploded.

You complete four rounds of a 400 m run, 24 back squats (185 lb / 125 lb) and 24 jerks (135 lb / 95 lb). That is 1,600 m of running, 96 back squats and 96 jerks. The squats are heavy for 24 reps, and the jerks need power from tired legs. Two bars set up side by side keep the workout moving.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Steady pace. Use the run to bring your breathing down before the squats."}, {"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "24", "tip": "Take the bar from a rack. Sets of 6 to 8 with short rests.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Jerks", "reps": "24", "tip": "Push jerk or split jerk from the front rack. Lock out overhead on every rep.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Two bars, so you never change plates", "Small sets on the squats", "Use your legs on every jerk"]'::jsonb,
   '["Load the squat bar in a rack and the jerk bar on the floor or in a second rack.", "Plan your squat sets, such as 4 sets of 6, and keep the rests short.", "On the jerks, dip straight down and drive hard with your legs before you push under the bar.", "Short sets of 4 to 6 jerks keep your shoulders fresh for later rounds.", "Hold the same run pace each round so the barbell work decides your time."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the back squat to 135 lb / 95 lb and the jerks to 95 lb / 65 lb. Use push presses or dumbbell push presses if the jerks are new to you. Cut the reps to 15 per round or do three rounds for a shorter workout.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Bruck workout?", "answer": "4 rounds for time of a 400 m run, 24 back squats (185 lb / 125 lb) and 24 jerks (135 lb / 95 lb)."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Bruck?", "answer": "96 back squats and 96 jerks, plus 1,600 m of running."}, {"question": "Can I push press instead of jerk?", "answer": "Yes, as a scaled version. Any style of jerk counts for the Rx version, as long as you lock the bar out overhead."}, {"question": "Who was Bruck?", "answer": "U.S. Coast Guard Petty Officer 3rd Class Nathan B. Bruckenthal, 24, of Smithtown, New York. He was killed on April 24, 2004, at the Khawr Al Amaya Oil Terminal off the coast of Iraq."}]'::jsonb,
