   'time',
   'Bulger honors Canadian Forces Cpl. Nicholas Bulger, 30, of Peterborough, Ontario, of the 3rd Battalion of Princess Patricia''s Canadian Light Infantry, based in Edmonton, Alberta. He died on July 3, 2009, while on patrol in the Zhari District of Afghanistan, when an improvised explosive device detonated near his vehicle.

You complete ten rounds of a 150 m run, 7 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 7 front squats (135 lb / 95 lb) and 7 handstand push-ups. That is 1,500 m of running and 70 reps of each movement. No single round is hard, but the pulling and pressing add up, and the short runs give you only a little time to recover.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "150 m", "tip": "Short and quick, but leave enough to start the pull-ups right away."}, {"name": "Chest-to-Bar Pull-Ups", "reps": "7", "tip": "Pull until your chest touches the bar. Break into 4 and 3 once your grip tires."}, {"name": "Front Squats", "reps": "7", "tip": "Clean the bar up each round, keep your elbows high and stay upright.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "7", "tip": "Head to the floor and arms locked out at the top. Small sets from the start."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Set up the bar, rig and wall close to the run start", "Break handstand push-ups before you fail", "Same pace every round"]'::jsonb,
   '["Keep the barbell, pull-up bar and wall space within a few steps of each other.", "On the chest-to-bar pull-ups, a tight kip and a strong pull to the chest save energy over 70 reps.", "Clean the bar into a solid front rack before your first front squat each round.", "Handstand push-ups tend to fall apart in later rounds, so break them early, such as 4 and 3.", "Aim for similar round times. Going hard in the first three rounds makes the last three much slower."]'::jsonb,
   'Use regular pull-ups or banded pull-ups in place of chest-to-bar, lower the front squat to 95 lb / 65 lb, and use pike push-ups or box pike push-ups for the handstand push-ups. Cut to six rounds for a shorter workout.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Bulger workout?", "answer": "10 rounds for time of a 150 m run, 7 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 7 front squats (135 lb / 95 lb) and 7 handstand push-ups."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Bulger?", "answer": "70 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 70 front squats and 70 handstand push-ups, plus 1,500 m of running."}, {"question": "What counts as a chest-to-bar pull-up?", "answer": "Your chest must touch the bar on every rep. It is harder than a regular pull-up, where the chin clears the bar."}, {"question": "Who was Bulger?", "answer": "Canadian Forces Cpl. Nicholas Bulger, 30, of the 3rd Battalion of Princess Patricia''s Canadian Light Infantry. He died on July 3, 2009, in the Zhari District of Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
